# CLEAR -- the VIC-II sixteen made readable, for protan eyes as well
# (Doc, 2026-10-06: "the red looks muddy, like a brown").
#
# Every colour a program writes text in reads at 4.5:1 or better on the
# blue, as normal eyes see it and as protan eyes do.  The blue is a little
# darker, which lifts everything on it.  Red goes pink -- to protan eyes a
# blue-grey, not the VIC-II red's dark olive -- and grey is lighter than it,
# so the two do not meet.  Orange goes towards yellow; purple and light
# blue lighter.  Yellow is a full yellow and light green a cooler one,
# green towards teal and cyan towards sky blue: to protan eyes the
# VIC-II's yellow and light green were one colour, and cyan the same as
# white.  Red and brown stay dark: they are backgrounds (white reads on
# both).  Load it with PALETTE LOAD CLEAR,
# or put that line in your /STARTUP.BAT.
#
# index rr gg bb, all hex.  A file only changes the entries it names.
#
COLOR 7 6
0 00 00 00
1 FF FF FF
2 CC 22 55
3 AA EE FF
4 DD 77 FF
5 33 CC 99
6 00 00 88
7 FF EE 00
8 FF 99 22
9 66 44 11
A FF 77 BB
B 33 33 33
C AA AA AA
D 99 FF 99
E 55 AA FF
F CC CC CC
